From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Naim <dnaim@cachyos.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:05:48 +0800
Subject: Revert "drm/gud: validate TV mode names before creating enum
 property"

This reverts commit da1ea35fea67ad841f4ada28dd61b41be65e5437.
This commit breaks compiling with clang 22.1.8 -O3.

Since the prior commit already mitigates the issue, reverting this
should be fine until clang gets updated in Arch Linux/CachyOS.

Signed-off-by: Eric Naim <dnaim@cachyos.org>
(cherry picked from commit d10310a163cefdadf7e42689243b15eef85a5435)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
index 8141c3a1e30ad95174130700f5c2672793d2c7df..5c0065c876a77f55fd9fc81a0fde94af5f35389c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -399,11 +399,8 @@ static int gud_connector_add_tv_mode(struct gud_device *gdrm, struct drm_connect
 	for (i = 0; i < num_modes; i++) {
 		char *mode = &buf[i * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN];
 
-		if (!memchr(mode, '\0', GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN)) {
-			ret = -EIO;
-			goto free;
-		}
-
+		/* The device is not trusted to NUL-terminate the name */
+		mode[GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN - 1] = '\0';
 		modes[i] = mode;
 	}
 
